======================================================================
6. GOLDBACH DECOMPOSITIONS IN RAPIDITY SPACE
======================================================================

  For even n, Goldbach decompositions: n = p + q, both prime.
  In rapidity: (rapidity(p), rapidity(q)) = (ln(p)/2, ln(q)/2).
  Note: rapidity(p) + rapidity(q) = ln(pq)/2, NOT ln(p+q)/2 = ln(n)/2.
  So the points do NOT lie on the line x+y = rapidity(n).
  Instead they satisfy: e^{2x} + e^{2y} = n (the EXPONENTIAL constraint).

