  MULTIPLICATIVE STRUCTURE IN RAPIDITY:
  The integers form a free abelian monoid under multiplication,
  generated by the primes. In rapidity space, this becomes an
  ADDITIVE monoid generated by {ln(p)/2 : p prime}.

  Perfect square <=> all rapidity components even
  Perfect cube   <=> all rapidity components divisible by 3
  k-th power     <=> all rapidity components divisible by k

